  "details": "With the current implementation of Content Gating this really isn't too big of an issue, but this will be in the future. The current Content gating allows for worlds and avatars to be blocked from you wearing or joining with the exception of Uploaded Avatars, I don't see that being too much of a problem, the only problem I see with it is when the Content Gating gets more normalized, mainly because when the new system roles out, if a NVA or V13+ gets a hold of an avatar and tags it with Sexually Suggestive, other NVA or V13+ will not be able to see it, but all V18+ will be able to. I feel like for Content Gated Avatars that you uploaded, they should be like Marketplace avatars and be purely client sided, either using the previous avatar you had, your fallback avatar, or the content gated placeholder to ensure safety. that or just remove the ability for NVA or V13+ to tag their stuff with sexually suggestive.",
